# Pagination — TokenRealty

## Defaults

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Default page size | 20 (`@PageableDefault(size = 20)`) |
| Maximum page size | 500 |
| Page index | 0-based (Spring Data) |

## Controller pattern

```java
@GetMapping
public Page<ListingResponse> list(
        @RequestParam(required = false) ListingStatus status,
        @PageableDefault(size = 20) Pageable pageable) {
    return listingService.findAll(status, pageable);
}
```

## Rules

* All collection GET endpoints accept `page`, `size`, `sort`
* Clamp `size` to max 500 at controller if accepting raw `@RequestParam int size`
* Service layer receives `Pageable` — do not re-clamp in every service method
* Return `Page<ResponseDto>` — never expose JPA entities in paginated responses
* Stable sort: default `createdAt,desc` or `id,asc` for deterministic pages
* High-volume tables (orders, transfers): require filter params (`buyerId`, `listingId`, date range) — no unbounded full scans in prod

